From: Orange Pi 5B Builder <pencil.bsp@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: egl/dri2: fail dmabuf export when the fd query fails

dri2_export_dma_buf_image_mesa() checks the return value of every
__DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB query except the one that matters most: it ignores
whether __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD succeeded, and returns EGL_TRUE regardless.
When the query fails, fds[i] is never written, so the caller gets back an
uninitialised stack slot as a file descriptor and is told the export
worked.

On RK3588 this is not theoretical. panfrost allocates offscreen render
targets from the device's exclusive VM, and panthor_gem_prime_export()
refuses to export those:

    /* We can't export GEMs that have an exclusive VM. */
    if (to_panthor_bo(obj)->exclusive_vm_root_gem)
            return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);

so drmPrimeHandleToFD() returns EINVAL for every such buffer. GTK4's GL
renderer calls eglExportDMABUFImageMESA() to turn a rendered texture into
a GdkDmabufTexture, is told it succeeded, and then reads the result
through a garbage descriptor. Every download path fails, GDK logs a
warning, and the caller keeps the uninitialised pixel buffer. Visibly,
gnome-initial-setup saves the generated user avatar as random memory and
the login screen shows noise.

Report the failure instead, closing any descriptor already exported. EGL
consumers already handle a refused export: GTK falls back to reading the
texture back with glReadPixels, which works fine on this hardware.

Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-09-14
---
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
@@ -2591,10 +2591,25 @@
           *    "If the number of fds is less than the number of planes, then
           *    subsequent fd slots should contain -1."
           */
-         if (i == 0 || is_disjoint)
-            dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD, &fds[i]);
-         else
+         if (i == 0 || is_disjoint) {
+            if (!dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD, &fds[i])) {
+               /* The driver refused to export this buffer -- panthor returns
+                * -EINVAL for any BO bound to an exclusive VM, which is what
+                * panfrost allocates offscreen render targets from. Reporting
+                * success here leaves fds[i] holding whatever the caller had
+                * on its stack, and every consumer then reads from a bogus fd.
+                */
+               for (int j = 0; j < i; j++)
+                  if (fds[j] >= 0)
+                     close(fds[j]);
+               if (i)
+                  dri2_destroy_image(image);
+               mtx_unlock(&dri2_dpy->lock);
+               return EGL_FALSE;
+            }
+         } else {
             fds[i] = -1;
+         }
       }
 
       if (strides && !dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_STRIDE, &strides[i]))
